      "content": "That makes sense, thanks. I've noticed a lot of the \"collectivist\" vs \"expressive\" distinction in the papers I'm reading, but it feels like it gets simplified sometimes.\n\nFor the sake of the literature review, I'm trying to see if there are more specific behavioral descriptors often used in these studies. For example, when we talk about that \"expressive\" temperament in Middle Eastern populations during stress, is it typically described in terms of being more confrontational or assertive in a workspace? And on the flip side, would the East Asian \"restraint\" be characterized more as being passive or perhaps just more stoic and quiet? I'm just trying to get the terminology right for my thesis.",
